---
import { BOT } from "@data/config";

import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "1 September 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Terms of Service"
    description="Terms governing the use of the AOO bot for tracking Albion Online Black Zone objectives on your Discord server."
>
    <main class="prose mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>

        <p class="text-muted-foreground">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

        <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>

        <p>
            By adding the AOO bot (Albion Online Objectives) to a Discord server, or by using any of
            its commands, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not add the bot and do
            not use it.
        </p>

        <p>
            These terms are an agreement between you and the bot's operator. They do not replace
            Discord's own terms, which continue to apply to your use of the platform.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What the service does</h2>

        <p>
            The AOO bot tracks end-game objectives in Albion Online — resource nodes, Cores and
            Vortexes located in the Black Zone. Members of your server report an objective, and the
            bot maintains a shared list showing when each one becomes available.
        </p>

        <p>The bot provides four commands:</p>

        <ul>
            <li><code>/add</code> — report a new objective</li>
            <li><code>/list</code> — display the server's tracked objectives</li>
            <li><code>/edit</code> — modify an objective already reported</li>
            <li><code>/remove</code> — delete an objective</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            The service is free of charge. It is an independent project and is not affiliated with,
            endorsed by, or sponsored by Sandbox Interactive GmbH, the developer of Albion Online, or
            by Discord.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Eligibility</h2>

        <p>
            You must have a Discord account in good standing and meet Discord's minimum age
            requirement for your country. Your use of the bot is also subject to the
            <a href="https://discord.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                Discord Terms of Service
            </a>
            and the
            <a href="https://discord.com/guidelines" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                Discord Community Guidelines
            </a>. Where these terms conflict with Discord's developer terms, Discord's terms prevail.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>

        <p>When using the bot, you agree not to:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>Submit deliberately false objective data to disrupt other players</li>
            <li>Automate or script command calls to generate abnormal request volumes</li>
            <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the bot, its database, or its infrastructure</li>
            <li>Use the bot to harass, spam, or otherwise harm other users</li>
            <li>Use the bot in a way that breaches Discord's terms or Albion Online's own rules</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            Server administrators are responsible for how the bot is used on their server, including
            deciding which members may modify or delete objectives.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Availability</h2>

        <p>
            The service is provided <strong>as is</strong> and <strong>as available</strong>, without
            warranty of any kind. We do not guarantee that it will be uninterrupted, error-free, or
            that objective data will be accurate — that data is submitted by players, not verified by
            us.
        </p>

        <p>
            The service may be suspended, modified, or discontinued at any time, including for
            maintenance, or because a change to Discord or to Albion Online makes it unworkable.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>

        <p>
            To the fullest extent permitted by law, the operator is not liable for any indirect or
            consequential loss arising from your use of the bot, including lost in-game time,
            resources or opportunities resulting from inaccurate, missing, or delayed objective data.
        </p>

        <p>
            Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded under applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Termination</h2>

        <p>
            You may stop using the service at any time by removing the bot from your server. Doing so
            ends all processing for that server; remaining objectives expire and are deleted
            automatically, as described in our
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
            We may restrict or withdraw access for a server that breaches section 4, or where
            continued operation would breach Discord's terms.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>

        <p>
            These terms may be updated as the service evolves. The date at the top of this page
            always reflects the current version, and material changes will be announced on the
            support Discord server. Continuing to use the bot after a change means you accept the
            revised terms.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Governing law</h2>

        <p>
            These terms are governed by French law. If you are a consumer resident in the European
            Union, you keep the protection of the mandatory provisions of the law of your country of
            residence.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Contact</h2>

        <p>For any question about these terms:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Support Discord server</strong> —
                <a href={BOT.discordInvite} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    join the server
                </a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Email</strong> —
                <a href={`mailto:${BOT.contactEmail}`}>{BOT.contactEmail}</a>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </main>
</BaseLayout>
